                <pb facs="0343" n="304" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v28/pg304"/>

                <head>126. Memorandum for the Record<anchor n="1" xml:id="d126-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1975-08-21">August 21, 1975</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>40 Committee Actions</item>
                </list>
                <p>Following the discussion at a 40 Committee meeting on 20 August 1975<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d126-f2"/> the Chairman of The 40 Committee raised the question of
                    additional funding of Angola operations with higher authority. The latter
                    approved an additional expenditure of [<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line
                        not declassified</hi>] and authority for the Director of Central
                    Intelligence to initiate action to obtain an appropriation of [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">less than 1 line not declassified</hi>] in anticipation
                    of continuing operational requirements.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">Rob Roy Ratliff</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <title>Executive Secretary</title>
                    <lb/>
                    <affiliation>The 40 Committee</affiliation>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
